  "slug": "yaner-dao-ling",
  "audio_url": "/audio/russian/13535_yaner-dao-ling.mp3",
  "english_paragraphs": [
    "Once upon a time, there was a man who saw a big clock at the door of someone else's house and wanted to steal it. But the bell was big and heavy, so he took a hammer and tried to break it into pieces, then steal it piece by piece. But the hammer striking the bell will make a loud sound that can be heard by everyone, and he will definitely be discovered. He thought again: If he covered his ears when ringing the bell, he would hear nothing! He felt that if he couldn't hear the sound, others wouldn't be able to hear it either. Then he struck the bell with a hammer while covering his ears. Many people heard the bell and came to catch the thief. This idiom is \"hiding one's ears and stealing the bell\". We often use this idiom to describe our behavior of deceiving ourselves."
  ],
  "english_full": "Once upon a time, there was a man who saw a big clock at the door of someone else's house and wanted to steal it. But the bell was big and heavy, so he took a hammer and tried to break it into pieces, then steal it piece by piece. But the hammer striking the bell will make a loud sound that can be heard by everyone, and he will definitely be discovered. He thought again: If he covered his ears when ringing the bell, he would hear nothing! He felt that if he couldn't hear the sound, others wouldn't be able to hear it either. Then he struck the bell with a hammer while covering his ears. Many people heard the bell and came to catch the thief. This idiom is \"hiding one's ears and stealing the bell\". We often use this idiom to describe our behavior of deceiving ourselves.",
  "russian_paragraphs": [
    "Оди́н раз была́ история о муже, который уви́дел большо́й часы́ у две́ри кого́-то и реши́л укра́сть их. Но ко́локол был большо́й и тяжёлый, поэ́тому он взя́л молото́к и попы́тался разбить его́ на кусо́чки, а затем укра́сть его́ кусо́к за кусо́чком."
  ],
  "reading_paragraphs": [
    "Odin raz byla istoriya o muzhe, kotoryy uvidel bol'shoy chasy u dveri kogo-to i reshil ukrast' ikh. No kolokol byl bol'shoy i tyazhelyy, poetomu on vzyal molotok i popytalsya razbity' yevo na kusochki, a zatem ukrast' yevo kusok za kusochkom."
  ],
